        "original_id": "7ddf7813-1092-5bce-99bf-e827cb4b6455",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: M. S. Swaminathan, Norman Borlaug, Gregory Conko\n- Topics: Green Revolution in India, genetically modified food, agricultural science, awards\n\nFacts:\n- During the Green Revolution in India, higher-yielding varieties of wheat were the main development.\n- Many scientists developed these higher-yielding wheat varieties, including Indian geneticist M. S. Swaminathan and American agronomist Norman Borlaug.\n- Norman Borlaug was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize, the Presidential Medal of Freedom, and the Congressional Gold Medal for his work.\n- In \"The Frankenfood Myth,\" Gregory Conko argues against over-regulation of genetically modified food.\n- \"The Frankenfood Myth\" features a foreword by Nobel Peace Prize-winner Norman Ernest Borlaug.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
